eepp NanoSVG security patches, applied 2026-10-25

Base: existing modified FLTK-derived snapshot. Exact upstream base is still
unestablished; do not replace it with master and discard eepp style/currentColor
or SVG-glyph integration changes.

Manual fixes:
- CVE-2026-88366 / upstream #294: reject non-finite arc endpoints and fall back
  to a line for invalid radii/rotation or non-finite intermediate angles and
  centers before the angle-to-int conversion.
- CVE-2026-88368 / upstream #292: validate finite edge geometry and rounded
  fixed-point coordinates before casting or consuming a pool entry. Compare
  against int bounds in double, since float(INT_MAX) rounds out of range.
  Reject edges whose scanline advancement would overflow; skip rejected
  edges without suppressing subsequent valid edges on that scanline.
- CVE-2026-88367 / upstream #293: validate stroke tessellation inputs, use
  double intermediates and cap the count at 1024 before converting to int.
  Extreme geometry may be omitted or approximated rather than invoking UB.

No new rasterizer allocations or public layout changes are introduced.

Rasterizer fixes, applied 2026-10-26 (found by fuzzing, no upstream reports):
- Single-stop gradients filled the color ramp from stops[0..255]; use stops[0].
- Dashed strokes are capped at NSVG__MAX_DASH_SEGMENTS (16384) per
  nsvgRasterizeXY call, tracked in NSVGrasterizer::dashSegments. Unbounded
  dashing could loop forever once dashes fell below coordinate precision.
- nsvg__clampf maps NaN to the lower bound; its callers index arrays with it.
- nsvg__roundJoin no longer converts a NaN segment count to int.
The dashSegments field is the only change to an internal struct.
Tests: src/tests/unit_tests/nanosvg_security_tests.cpp, plus existing image,
SVG widget and font rendering tests. .clang-format preserves snapshot style.

Reports:
https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg/issues/292
https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg/issues/293
https://github.com/memononen/nanosvg/issues/294
